    "interpretation": "The 210 BOLD barcode documents include six named species values plus five missing species values under the same BIN. The Philippines subset itself contains Arius dispar and Arius manillensis labels. This establishes that the BIN is not a safe one-to-one species identifier for this source chain; it does not establish which of the other names, if any, is a misidentification. The exact BPC001-13 record remains source-reported as Arius dispar by morphology, but this BIN export is not an independent identification of that specimen and does not resolve the separate GBIF Backbone mapping to Netuma thalassina."
